        "event": "Coastal Flood Advisory",
        "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
        "senderName": "NWS San Diego CA",
        "headline": "Coastal Flood Advisory issued November 5 at 1:31AM PST until November 10 at 12:00PM PST by NWS San Diego CA",
        "description": "* WHAT...Minor to locally moderate coastal flooding expected.\nDangerous rip currents and elevated surf expected along west-\nfacing beaches.\n\n* WHERE...San Diego County Coastal Areas and Orange County\nCoastal Areas.\n\n* WHEN...From 4 AM Friday to noon PST Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of lots, parks, and roads with only\nisolated road closures expected.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Coastal residents and managers of\ninfrastructure in the advisory area should prepare for rising\nwater and take appropriate action to protect life and property.\nHighest tides will occur in the late morning each day. Observed\nhigh tides are 1.3 to 1.6 feet above astronomical tide\npredictions. Surf will increase starting Monday, but there is\nuncertainty in details at this time.",
        "instruction": "If travel is required, allow extra time as some roads may be\nclosed. Do not drive around barricades or through water of\nunknown depth. Take the necessary actions to protect flood-prone\nproperty.",
